The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
skb = skb_realloc_headroom(skb, MLXSW_TXHDR_LEN);
if (!skb) {
    dev_kfree_skb_any(skb_orig);
    return NETDEV_TX_OK;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the original socket buffer (`skb_orig`) is only released in the error path when `skb_realloc_headroom()` fails (i.e., returns `NULL`). If the reallocation is successful, the original skb is not freed, leading to a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
dev_consume_skb_any(skb_orig);
```
Reason:
This statement is added to the main path after the successful reallocation of the skb. It ensures that the original skb is properly released when a new skb is allocated, preventing the memory leak that occurs when the original skb is not freed.

